<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bilyar</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bilyar was a major city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tatarstan">Tatarstan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, east of the Volga. In the 11th and 12th centuries it served as the capital, a fortified trading centre covering several square kilometres and one of the largest cities of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> destroyed it in 1236, and its remains are an archaeological site near the village of Bilyarsk.</p></div>
